==Notes==
<references group="nb"/>
* <small>All matches played during the tenure of [[Jimmy McStay]] were unofficial war-time games. Although there were still competitions; [[Southern Football League (Scotland)|Scottish Southern League]], [[Southern League Cup (Scotland)|Scottish Southern League Cup]] and [[Summer Cup (Scottish football)|Summer Cup]], none of these competitions are recognised as official.</small><ref>{{cite web|title=The War Years: 1940–49|url=http://www.football50.co.uk/the-war-years-1940-49/|website=Jim Craig's Football 50|access-date=16 January 2017|archive-date=18 January 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170118050109/http://www.football50.co.uk/the-war-years-1940-49/|url-status=live}}</ref>
* <small>[[Sean Fallon (footballer)|Sean Fallon]]'s season as caretaker manager in season 1975–76 was due to [[Jock Stein]]'s recuperation from injuries sustained in a serious car accident.</small><ref name="ipost" /><ref name="cw282" />
* <small>[[Neil Lennon]] initially took over from [[Tony Mowbray]] as manager in March 2010 on a temporary basis, but was appointed as full-time manager in June 2010.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gardner |first1=Neil |last2=Gordon |first2=Phil |title=Celtic confirm Neil Lennon as their new manager |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/football/article/celtic-confirm-neil-lennon-as-their-new-manager-bgcl7fqp8rf |newspaper=[[The Times]] |date=9 June 2010 |access-date=27 January 2018 |archive-date=28 January 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180128132718/https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/celtic-confirm-neil-lennon-as-their-new-manager-bgcl7fqp8rf |url-status=live }}</ref></small>

